# shadcn/ui (apps/web)

This app uses shadcn (`components.json`, `src/components/ui/`). **Do not reinvent what shadcn already provides.**

## Before building UI primitives

1. Check `apps/web/src/components/ui/` for an existing component.
2. If missing, check the [shadcn registry](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components) and add it from `apps/web`:
   `bunx shadcn@latest add <component> --yes`
3. Compose with `@/components/ui/*` (e.g. `Separator`, `Button`, `Dialog`) instead of one-off Tailwind patterns (`divide-x`, raw modal markup, etc.) when the shadcn component fits.

## Examples

- Column/section dividers → `Separator` (`orientation="vertical"`), not `divide-x`
- Actions → `Button`, not unstyled `<button>` with duplicated classes
- Overlays, menus, forms → use the matching shadcn component if one exists

Match existing component style in `src/components/ui/` (Base UI primitives, `cn` from `cn`).
